  "worked_solution": "To make our prediction, we proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we start at $y=80$ on the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/e5923b6c9f0ac4dcf2aee35e67877c425b44f81830bb9f0865c5e21acf81e3f4.png)\n\n- Then, we move right until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/613849314df8014335f7493f9b6b64cb4f2ecd1e585593416f416f1854e12ffa.png)\n\n- Finally, we move down until we intersect the $x$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/4523e742266e3f2d2e759c6e65eb2a7f2bd31e8f4b8473b8e6bfbabec067c9d9.png)\n\nTherefore, when $y=80,$ we obtain $x≈15.$",
